// A buffer byte chosen when the program RUNS: `Frame[BytePos]` with BytePos a
// #param, a variable or any expression. The access is the byte at position 0
// and an OP_SETOX in bits mode moves it by 8*index bits; its length is the
// number of bytes the view can reach, so the same bounds check as an array's.
//
// The case it is for: which car a DL1200 sits in is a frame id, a byte and a
// mask -- settings, written after delivery, never compiled in.
#param CanId:32 unsigned = 0x30
#param BytePos = 1
#param BitMask = 0x40

#buffer Frame:8 in can 0x31
#in INIT
Frame.id = CanId
#end

#local HighBeam:1 = (Frame[BytePos] & BitMask) == BitMask
#variable Hits = 0
Hits = Hits + 1 ? Frame.rx && HighBeam

// A variable and an expression as the index, read and written.
#buffer B:4
#variable I = 1
#variable R1 = 0
#variable R2 = 0
#variable Whole = 0
B[I] = 0x22 ? 1
B[I+2] = 0x44 ? 1
R1 = B[I] ? 1
R2 = B[2*I+1] ? 1
Whole = B ? 1
